From: haiku-rpi
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: bcm2835_sdhci: no 1 ms wait after each command on the BCM2711 EMMC2

SDHCI_QUIRK_WAIT_SEND_CMD (udelay(1000) after every command) works around the
BCM2835 Arasan controller. The BCM2711 EMMC2 does not need it -- Linux drives it
with sdhci-iproc, whose bcm2711 data has only SDHCI_QUIRK_MULTIBLOCK_READ_ACMD12
-- and with CMD18 + CMD12 per read it cost ~2 ms of every block read: an EFI
loader reading 4.7 MB in 728 reads spent 2.5 s in them.
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhci.c
index efa4d14f..f0759e2b 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhci.c
@@ -211,7 +211,14 @@ static int bcm2835_sdhci_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 	host->name = dev->name;
 	host->ioaddr = (void *)(uintptr_t)base;
 	host->quirks = SDHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_VOLTAGE | SDHCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_R1B |
-		SDHCI_QUIRK_WAIT_SEND_CMD | SDHCI_QUIRK_NO_HISPD_BIT;
+		SDHCI_QUIRK_NO_HISPD_BIT;
+	/*
+	 * The 1 ms wait after every command is for the BCM2835's Arasan
+	 * controller; the BCM2711's EMMC2 does not need it (Linux's sdhci-iproc
+	 * has no such quirk for it), and it costs ~2 ms of every block read.
+	 */
+	if (clock_id != BCM2835_MBOX_CLOCK_ID_EMMC2)
+		host->quirks |= SDHCI_QUIRK_WAIT_SEND_CMD;
 	host->max_clk = emmc_freq;
 	host->voltages = MMC_VDD_32_33 | MMC_VDD_33_34 | MMC_VDD_165_195;
 	host->ops = &bcm2835_ops;
